Z||000001||theogre||08-05-2000||08:05 PM||||check the RPO label on the fender if it's still there.... there are a few places to look up the codes. no I don't have those links handy.<P>Likely it got the stiffer suspension at the least. May also have the 3 turn (turns of steering wheel lock to lock) steering instead of the 3.5 turn.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||08-05-2000||09:53 PM||||In 84 there was an econo coupe.  As its name implies AC and auto were not available. The sport coupe had some wheel options and tire options.<P>In 85, the econo coupe was back. Optional door pockets in vinyl.<P>The sport coupe wheels and tire options, door pockets in seat vinyl. Option for v6.<P>In reading over the "Fiero Spotter's Guide" it appears that the sport coupe had more option packages available than the base coupe.  No mention of suspension upgrades.  Maybe if you got the v6 you'd get a different suspension.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||08-05-2000||11:13 PM||||The Sport Coupes had the 14" tech wheels and the stiffer springs (handling package) and more options then the coupes. The coupes had a choice of steel wheels or the 13" finned wheels.||||reg||1
